  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mi>y</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be the solution of the differential equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Then, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mi>e</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to",
